  "description": "The National Forest Explorer (NFE) is the ideal bike for long days of spirited riding on dirt roads. While designed to carry a small load over the front wheel for day supplies, the NFE also handles well with low-riders and a rear saddle bag for overnighting. Unlike many heavy \"adventure bikes\" sold by larger manufacturers, the NFE is light and responsive, built with a double-butted front triangle and 4130 rear triangle.\n\nThe geometry is optimized for experienced riders who prefer nimble handling and a light steering input. The fork is a straight unicrown construction with a handmade direct-mount disc tab.\n\nFor more information about the history of this bike, check out this article in Out There Monthly.",
